The file patches the real Go source of debug/pe/symbol.go.

The real file reads the package unsafe 2 times. Each 1 reads the 18 bytes of a
COFFSymbol through the type COFFSymbolAuxFormat5. The 2 types hold the same
layout. Thus each field of the second type stands at a fixed offset of the
first 1.

The read of an aux symbol needs no conversion at all. binary.Read of a
COFFSymbolAuxFormat5 takes the same 18 bytes as binary.Read of a COFFSymbol. It
also writes each byte at the same offset. Thus the patch reads a COFFSymbol.

COFFSymbolReadSectionDefAux gives a copy, and not a view of the entry of
COFFSymbols. Each field holds the number that Go reads on a little-endian
machine. Read docs/parity.md.

